<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-2709] High contention on a cache key leads to excsessive thread stack usage</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2709</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Currently &lt;tt&gt;GridCacheMvccManager#onOwnerChanged&lt;/tt&gt; callback notifies listeners synchronously. This means that the call stack size for a transaction commit is proportional to the size of MVCC candidates queue. On a big enough queue size this leads to a StackOverflowError (see the file attached).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I suggest the &lt;tt&gt;GridCacheMvccManager:158&lt;/tt&gt; line be executed asynchronously after some (3-5) nested calls.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The change should be properly benchmarked.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12941260">IGNITE-2709</key>
            <summary>High contention on a cache key leads to excsessive thread stack usage</summary>
